+\textbf{Contribution of the Dependency Graph.}
+To isolate the dependency graph from context propagation, we compare $\tool{}_{\textit{full}}$ with $\tool{}_{\textit{win}}$, which uses the five most recent statements with the same object summaries, and $\tool{}_{\textit{all}}$, which provides all preceding statements and the complete context.
+As shown in Table~\ref{tab:ablation_depgraph}, $\tool{}_{\textit{full}}$ achieves the highest execution validity (0.661 vs. 0.599 and 0.643) with 11.9\% and 72.3\% fewer input tokens per statement, whereas only 22.6\% and 4.2\% of the predecessors provided by $\tool{}_{\textit{win}}$ and $\tool{}_{\textit{all}}$ are dependency-relevant.
